  "method_card": {
   "steps": [
    "CF: add running totals and plot at upper class boundaries",
    "Read Q1, median, Q3 from the CF curve at n/4, n/2, 3n/4",
    "Box plots: draw using the five-number summary",
    "Histograms: frequency = frequency density × class width"
   ],
   "title": "Cumulative Frequency, Box Plots & Histograms",
   "content": "<p><strong>Cumulative frequency (CF):</strong> Running total of frequencies. Plot at <strong>upper class boundaries</strong> and join with a smooth S-shaped curve. Read off: <strong>median</strong> at \\(n/2\\), <strong>Q1</strong> at \\(n/4\\), <strong>Q3</strong> at \\(3n/4\\). <strong>IQR</strong> = Q3 − Q1.</p><p><strong>Box plots:</strong> Show the <strong>five-number summary</strong>: min, Q1, median, Q3, max. The box spans the IQR. Compare two distributions by comparing medians (average) and IQRs (consistency).</p><p><strong>Histograms:</strong> <strong>Frequency density</strong> = frequency ÷ class width. The <strong>area</strong> of each bar = frequency. Unequal class widths require frequency density on the y-axis.</p>",
   "example": "<p><strong>CF of 80 values: Q1 at 20th = 30, Median at 40th = 42, Q3 at 60th = 55.</strong></p><p>IQR = 55 − 30 = 25.</p>"
  },
